1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,000
This video is for you to introduce the relevant update of the chain.

2
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:11,000
In the previous version, when you need to change the attribute of a more than 3D chain on a piece of clothing,

3
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:15,000
you must choose one by one and modify each chain.

4
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:20,000
In the 2025.1 version, the object window added a new chain selection card.

5
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:26,000
You can manage the chain according to the sample, and store and apply it to the entire chain.

6
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:31,000
First of all, when you see the object window, a new chain selection is added here.

7
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:37,000
From the current version, the operation related to the chain will be controlled by this selection card.

8
00:00:37,000 --> 00:00:43,000
Press the increase button in the upper right corner to create a new default chain pattern.

9
00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:46,000
Then apply the newly created chain to the clothing.

10
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:50,000
First, select the 3D chain to be applied in the 3D window.

11
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:55,000
Then press the application button on the right side of the new chain in the object window.

12
00:00:55,000 --> 00:00:56,000
You can apply it.

13
00:00:56,000 --> 00:01:04,000
If you first select a chain, then click the application button in the upper right corner of the object window,

14
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:07,000
a new default chain will be created at the bottom.

15
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:11,000
And it will be applied directly to the selected 3D chain.

16
00:01:11,000 --> 00:01:17,000
The copy will copy a similar one with a chain pattern.

17
00:01:17,000 --> 00:01:21,000
Select a chain in the object window.

18
00:01:21,000 --> 00:01:25,000
In the attribute editor at the bottom,

19
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:28,000
you can modify the overall shape of the chain.

20
00:01:28,000 --> 00:01:34,000
Including the basic information of the chain, the type of the chain, and the size of the chain.

21
00:01:34,000 --> 00:01:36,000
You can see the changes.

22
00:01:36,000 --> 00:01:42,000
The corresponding chain in the 3D window will also change.

23
00:01:42,000 --> 00:01:45,000
While maintaining the overall shape,

24
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:50,000
you can also select the details of various components such as the editor, the head, and the chain.

25
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:56,000
When you use the option to press and hold the head, the chain, or the stop component,

26
00:01:56,000 --> 00:01:59,000
it will immediately select the entire chain component.

27
00:01:59,000 --> 00:02:02,000
At this time, if you press and hold the button again to edit the object,

28
00:02:02,000 --> 00:02:04,000
it will only select a specific object.

29
00:02:04,000 --> 00:02:08,000
If the selected object is divided into two or more grid,

30
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:12,000
then press and hold the button again to select only a specific object.

31
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:17,000
Here, click the chain part again to edit the size of the chain separately.

32
00:02:17,000 --> 00:02:22,000
After the modification, the chain component will be selected again.

33
00:02:22,000 --> 00:02:28,000
You can press and hold the button again to edit a certain material color separately.

34
00:02:28,000 --> 00:02:30,000
You can also unify the modification.

35
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:33,000
You can also select the chain and cloth to modify the material color, etc.

36
00:02:33,000 --> 00:02:36,000
It is the same as the previous operation.

37
00:02:36,000 --> 00:02:41,000
You can also save the design chain pattern as a GPS format,

38
00:02:41,000 --> 00:02:43,000
and use it for other projects.

39
00:02:43,000 --> 00:02:46,000
In the object window, select the chain to be saved.

40
00:02:47,000 --> 00:02:51,000
Click the save button at the top of the property editor to save the file.

41
00:02:51,000 --> 00:02:56,000
The saved ZPS chain file can be opened and opened by the button next to it at any time,

42
00:02:56,000 --> 00:02:59,000
and re-loaded in other projects.

43
00:02:59,000 --> 00:03:02,000
Here, open another clothing project file.

44
00:03:02,000 --> 00:03:04,000
In the object window, select the chain,

45
00:03:04,000 --> 00:03:07,000
find the open icon in the property editor,

46
00:03:07,000 --> 00:03:10,000
and select the ZPS file to be saved.

47
00:03:10,000 --> 00:03:13,000
You can see the new sample in the chain selection card list,

48
00:03:13,000 --> 00:03:17,000
and it is also applied to the 3D clothing chain.

49
00:03:17,000 --> 00:03:19,000
In addition,

50
00:03:19,000 --> 00:03:24,000
you can press and hold the right button on the unused chain in the object window,

51
00:03:24,000 --> 00:03:27,000
and you can rename, delete, and reset it.

52
00:03:27,000 --> 00:03:32,000
It is an effective way to clean up the list by deleting all unused chains.

53
00:03:32,000 --> 00:03:35,000
You can see the new sample in the object window,

54
00:03:35,000 --> 00:03:38,000
and it is also applied to the 3D clothing chain.

55
00:03:38,000 --> 00:03:41,000
You can see the new sample in the object window,

56
00:03:41,000 --> 00:03:44,000
and it is also applied to the 3D clothing chain.

